.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taurctl-request-file 1  "taurctl-request-file " 
.SH NAME
taurctl\-request\-file \- File a request against a package base
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaurctl request file\fR <\fB\-\-kind\fR> [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-into\fR] <\fB\-\-comment\fR> [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPKGBASE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
File a request against a package base
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI<KIND>\fR
orphan, deletion, merge, or adoption
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Server URL (overrides TAUR_SERVER and the config file)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Config directory (default: $TAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl)
.TP
\fB\-\-into\fR \fI<INTO>\fR
Target package base for merge requests
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print raw JSON
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin instead of prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPKGBASE\fR>

